{"units": [{"id": "ego-note11", "translation": "Also Sept. 920. Pers. 633, 638. Ag. 458, 1401. Ch. 139. Eum. 779, 809. Suppl. 347, [785], 983. Fr. 92 Ἀτρέως πολυκοίρανε μάνθανέ μου [son of Atreus, ruler of many, learn from me] (alii μοι [to me]) παῖ [child]."}, {"id": "ego-note12", "translation": "With a preposition"}, {"id": "ego-note13", "translation": "to avoid a tribrach, for ὑπὲρ ἐμοῦ [on my behalf]. On this, compare what I said in Lexicon Sophocleum p. 134."}, {"id": "ego-note14", "translation": "Dative ἐμοί [to me]"}, {"id": "ego-note15", "translation": "Pr. 97, 191, 209, 260, 331, 338, 343, 616, 629, 631, 747, 782, 785, 874, 901, 938, 1043, 1089. Sept. 282, 979, 997, 998, 1043. Pers. 246, 351, 545, 631, 942. Ag. 316, 598, 811, 840, 882, 892, 905, 920, 924, 931, 943, 965, 1055, 1150, 1166, 1204, 1206, 1350, 1377, 1412, 1417, 1436, 1446, 1471, 1481, 1610, 1662. Ch. 75, 85, 112, 124, 183, 199, 239, 243, 522, 541, 543, 701, 732, 909, 1005, 1030, 1058. Eum. [119 φίλοις γάρ εἰσιν, οὐκ ἐμοὶ, προσίκτορες [for they are friends, not to me, suppliants]. Thus Hermann for ἐμοῖς [to my].] 155, 173, 288, 298, 304, 401, 434, 471, [481], 793, 829, 833, 850. Suppl. 249, 277, 310, 505, 602."}, {"id": "ego-note16", "translation": "where it is correctly written ἀμφ᾿ ἐμοί [around me], which should also be restored at Ch. 220 for ἀμφί μοι [around me]: for the preposition requires the orthotone form, on which I spoke in Lexicon Soph. p. 134b."}, {"id": "ego-note17", "translation": "Enclitic dative form μοι [to me]"}, {"id": "ego-note18", "translation": "Pr. 16, 63, 102, 107, 127, 197, 216, 271, 274, 294, 393, 535, 555, 584, 644, 742, 755, 777, 818, 935, 950, 1041. Sept. 71, 180, 223, 260, 480, 695. Pers. 114, 164, 170, 172, 181, 333, 519, 638, 705, 973, 987, 1048, 1056, 1067. Ag. 33, 494, 799, 936, 971, 1256, 1317, 1346, 1434, [1472], 1494, 1518, 1574, 1670. Ch. 2, 122, 140, 156, 181, 185, 193, 216, 240, 245, 280, 410, 417, 480, 489, 573, 584, 744, 783, 903, 987, 1010, 1040, 1041. Eum. 284, 393, 442, 594, 609, 747, 894, 898, 899, 971. Suppl. 319, 324, 349, 737, 792, 797, 810, 1054. Fr. 184, 201."}, {"id": "ego-note19", "translation": "Accusative ἐμέ [me]"}, {"id": "ego-note20", "translation": "Pr. 572, 665, 781, 872, 963, 974. Sept. 248, 253. Pers. 915. Ag. 586, 918, 925, 1269, 1275, 1537. Ch. 130, 225, 228, 252. Eum. 837, 838, 870, 871, 1003. Suppl. 996. Fr. 281, 4."}, {"id": "ego-note21", "translation": "Enclitic accusative form με [me]"}, {"id": "ego-note22", "translation": "Pr. 92, 115, 119, 132, 152, 172, 223, 227, 268, 289, 347, 382, 384, 387 100 437, 567, 576, 577, 585, 594, 598, 605, 625, 640, 670, 684, 877, 880, 894, 903, 976, 986, 990, 995, 1001, 1006, 1063, 1066, 1093. Sept. 81, 253, 715, 834, 873, 1005. Pers. 161, 688. Ag. 270, 546, 590, 946, 1087, 1138, 1202, 1215, 1240, 1243, 1260, 1270, 1390, 1403, 1499, 1605. Ch. 18, 45, 116, [277], 463, 695, 913, 1034. Eum. 30, 35, 36, 253, 305, 321, 323, 731, 736, 756, 761, 842, 845, 875, 878, 892, 896, 900, 902. Suppl. 116, 136, 144, 379, 397, 422, 456, 509, 714, 736, 786, 819, 894, 896, 1061. Fr. 133, 155 (where καί με [and me]). 238, 244, 302."}, {"id": "ego-note23", "translation": "There are two examples of the dual number,"}, {"id": "ego-note24", "translation": "and in the verses of the interpolator"}]}